        "original_id": "f1664522-9271-5fde-8ff1-3c0344e48bba",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Concepts: Dewey Lake Monster, Bigfoot, Sasquatch, cryptids\n- Places: Dewey Lake, Dowagiac, Michigan, Pacific Northwest\n- Topics: American folklore, reported sightings\n\nFacts:\n- In June 1964, the Dewey Lake Monster first gained wide notoriety after several reported sightings near Dewey Lake in Dowagiac, Michigan.\n- The Dewey Lake Monster is described as a large bipedal creature about 10 feet tall and weighing about 500 pounds.\n- The Dewey Lake Monster is also referred to as the Michigan Bigfoot and the Sister Lakes Sasquatch.\n- Bigfoot, also known as Sasquatch, is a cryptid in American folklore that is described as a simian-like creature said to inhabit forests, especially in the Pacific Northwest.",
